      <div>Kuza Cave in Jambiani is a sacred freshwater limestone cavern system formed over millennia, used for centuries by locals for spiritual rituals, ceremonies, and traditional medicine. Visitors can swim in crystal-clear turquoise pools, learn about Swahili cosmology and traditional healing practices from local guides, and participate in cultural workshops including drumming and cooking. Community-run; all fees support village development projects, education, and conservation. Combine with seaweed farm visit for a full cultural day.</div>
